The high energy prtls escaping from upstream will be marked with the tag "idle". The position and velocity of which will not be updated, and their charge will be ignored. 

Once they are marked as idle, a returning timescale will be calculated. Every timestep, the velocity will be subtracted by dt. Once remaining time < 0, idle prtls will be re-injected into the box, with v=-v. Every time prtl is marked as idle, a thermal prtl with u = u_drift will be injected to keep neutrality. Every time prtl is re-injected, a thermal prtl with opposite charge will be injected. This should be saved in ckpt. This will ensure prtls reinjected have the same ID.  

What is modified: 
	1. Adding a prtl tag type: idle in global/global.h
	 
